Yeah. You know, it's like the Nazis use the pit pistols, the, the gangsters use the Tommy gun.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.260
Why is, why does he have access to these?

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.760
And I get that like, cause it's boring to just use your fists to punch everything, but

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:59.920
all of these weapons share one singular ammo pool as well.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:03.640
And obviously like the more powerful, like if you have the bazooka, it takes more ammo

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:04.740
than it would the pistol.

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:06.480
Yeah. You just tape some bullets together.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.860
But like, you know, the fist doesn't cost any ammo cause otherwise you wouldn't have

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:13.940
any way of attacking. And that's also just like a weird concept to have your fist cost ammo.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:15.440
They would cost stamina if anything.

00:14:15.720 --> 00:14:16.840
But what do you think of that?

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:21.740
What do you think of that universal ammo versus specific ammo, uh, mechanic?

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:25.840
Cause in most games, when you have a gun, you have the ammo for that gun.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.960
And then if you pick up the machine gun, you have the ammo for the machine gun.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:31.800
What do you think of that shared pool mechanic that we have in this game?

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:33.160
I think it's okay.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:40.300
I don't think this game needs, I don't think it was going for a, like a, like a survival

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:42.420
horror, like watch your ammo thing.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.940
Like, uh, and I know that that's not the only case that that would be, but I didn't have

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:48.860
a problem with it.

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.340
It's ammo is pretty plenty plentiful.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:58.640
Um, and it, it, you could probably get, get away with not using the weapons at all.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:00.740
Cause this is a kind of easy game.

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:02.520
So I'm not, I'm not worried about it.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:09.640
Um, yeah, I think that it, it didn't bother me in this game because I felt it was a little

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:14.480
for whatever reason, I know it's just pressing select, but like it was just a little clunky

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.780
to change weapons while I'm like in the middle of a fight.

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:20.720
So at least I didn't have to also change weapons and think about how much ammo was in this other

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.140
weapon. I could just be, I had to, I had to head cannon it.

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:29.840
Like I was just changing the settings on my current gun, but using the same ammo, which

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.160
obviously isn't what's happening.

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.180
Right. I don't think I'm advocating for like, I'm not advocating for anybody to really do it,

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:39.320
but I even like the call of duties of the world don't need like universal ammo for all

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:43.960
the weapons. But it is interesting to think of like an unreal tournament or something that's like maybe a

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:49.540
little more, um, uh, you know, less grounded, uh, and just having it be like, Hey, if you

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:54.620
can find the real tournament, less grounded, less grounded.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.280
I don't know what it is about, uh, unreal tournament.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.420
There's just something less grounded than D day.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.420
They never really got that D day level figured out.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:10.380
But no, I know what you mean.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.300
Yes. Thank you.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:19.060
And then, you know, the, the jet pack having a fuel meter, probably a necessary evil, uh,

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:21.800
in the game. Like you can't just be flying all the time.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:27.360
It's the same reason why in super Mario brothers three, you can't just like constantly, uh, you

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:32.680
know, be flying as the, as raccoon Mario, you have to build up enough speed and things

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:38.880
can stop you. But I do feel like if we're going to compare the two games somehow, like super Mario brothers

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:45.000
three figured out something about the layout of its levels where flight was like more freeing

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.900
than the rocketeer is.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.040
And that's just strange.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:52.720
Like, I think it comes down to the fact that the rocketeer game takes place mostly like

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:54.740
inside and around buildings.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:58.000
So there's a lot of like, you're not going to launch it.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.800
You're not going to be in on a jet pack inside a building unless you need to like reach a specific

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:05.300
platform, but even then you're not going to like fly over the entire level.

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:12.400
It just seems like, you know, it's weird for the rocketeer to not like take the lessons

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:17.040
from super Mario brothers three on flight and be like, there's a way to handle this where

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:18.760
it doesn't just skip over the whole level.

00:17:18.940 --> 00:17:26.980
Maybe at this point it's more like laziness, not laziness, but, uh, like, Oh, we, well, we

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.820
kind of have this idea of this action game.

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:37.500
And when we play test having unlimited fuel or whatever, you just skip the whole thing.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:40.360
And it's, it's, it's hard to balance.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.560
So that's how I assume it might've gone.

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:47.920
Do you think it's like, I know this is, I don't know anything about the development of

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:53.400
this game. So it might be silly to ask if it feels like the rocket was added as an afterthought.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:54.920
Like, was this a different game?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:18:00.420
And then they, because it's just, you'd think there'd be like more enemies that are flying

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:08.940
or shooting up at you or like, I don't know, more obstacles up to stop you from, you know,

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.160
just flying over.

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:13.820
There are eventually like guys with, I don't know if they're, they're clearly not the

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:17.600
rocketeers jet pack, but they have like their own method of, of doing that.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:21.040
And like those, you know, those are enemies that kind of get in the way, but you're right.

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:26.960
For the most part, you can just like, provided you have the fuel, just hover over enemies and

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.040
it's completely, it does not matter at all.

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:34.780
I don't think it was an afterthought, but I do think it was something that they, it's

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:39.340
like, oh, we just need to, we need to get this in here somewhere for it to be rocketeer.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:44.880
And it was just kind of, it wasn't a very graceful way to do it.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:51.920
Yeah. Maybe there should have been like, you know, other levels that not, not, not that they felt

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:55.420
like mini games or anything, but there should have been some kind of flight levels as well.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:59.800
In addition to, you know, like dodge all this shit instead of fight all these enemies.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:00.940
enemies. I agree.

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:05.520
Cause there's a lot of enemies that they do just kind of, some of them will just spawn

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.340
right into you too.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.180
I hate that in game design.

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:14.340
Uh, but there are just like a lot of enemies on the screen and they, they aren't consequential.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:17.300
Like they are just kind of like, you know, you hit them twice or whatever and that'll

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:22.820
take care of them. Or if you have the gun, probably just one, but it's not, it's not a great way to feel

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.060
when playing the game that it's like, oh, I just wish I had the jet pack so I could skip

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:27.180
over all this bullshit.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.440
Like you don't want to be thinking that in the game.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:34.780
Well, especially because like a lot of the, like a lot of the enemies, there is some weird

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:39.880
like lining up issues where it's like a lot of times like, oh, they're standing behind

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:42.600
something, but I can't really fire over it unless I jump.

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.260
But if I jump, I jump way too high.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.160
So I don't have to shoot on my way down.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.540
Or there's like times where like, oh, I can't squat and shoot this guy.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:54.300
I can stand. But when I stand, like, it's just like not enough to reach him, but then I'm vulnerable.

00:19:54.300 --> 00:19:59.760
There's like weird things that make it kind of clunky in that sense, which makes me do

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:01.320
like want to skip over the enemies.

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:04.220
And I know Sean earlier, you said that this is kind of an easy game.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.460
I really disagree.

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.920
I had a really hard time with this game.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:07.880
I'm very bad at it.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:13.700
I think I got like the second level and then I watched the playthrough of the rest of it

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:15.620
because I just could not get like...

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:18.100
Were you trying to play fast by any chance, Joe?

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:19.940
Maybe a little bit at first.

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:23.360
I'm sure I slowed down once I kept dying, but I was really...

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:26.580
I think if you slow down, it's a little, it's just easier for...

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:29.720
And I'm not talking about like slow down, like crawl or anything.

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:34.880
But I noticed that I was just taking damage that I didn't need to be taking by trying

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:37.840
to run through these levels because of the way enemies spawn.

00:20:38.020 --> 00:20:41.900
Yeah. You just wind up taking a lot of like hits and then you just don't have enough health

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:43.120
for the actual fights.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:47.020
Yeah, there was definitely like a level of like, I know that I can get this guy without

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:50.660
getting hit if I take a stack, take a step, duck, take a step, duck.

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:51.940
And that's exactly what I was doing.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.180
Take a step, duck, take a step, duck.

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:56.460
And I think I did start skipping that sometimes because I was like, all right, I can get to this

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:59.400
guy before I have to do all that nonsense and then I would get hit.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:04.580
So like, yeah, whether it's like because of its difficulty or because like I don't, wasn't

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:07.340
having the patience to do what the game was asking me to do.

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.620
But like either way, it was just like I wasn't getting very far.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:13.720
One thing I did like about this game was the environmental design.

00:21:14.200 --> 00:21:16.720
Say more. Um, I don't know.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:23.100
I feel like a lot of these games have a couple pallets that they throw onto like, you know,

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:29.860
like repeating walls and, and, uh, whatever the textures that you actually walk on.

00:21:30.020 --> 00:21:32.020
And this, this game does have that.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:37.860
Like there's several levels where you're like in what feels like, well, there's one level

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:40.040
that's like an endless meat freezer.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:49.720
Um, which is really funny, but you also have like some actual like recognizable, uh, level

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:55.320
or like environments from the movie, uh, that actually look really nice with like the pixel

00:21:55.320 --> 00:22:02.020
art. And like you, you're in this club that, that has the stage and there's like, you, you walk

00:22:02.020 --> 00:22:06.840
through the, um, through the tables and on the chandeliers.

00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:11.300
And, um, when you're in the forest, it looks very pretty.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:18.140
And I don't think that there was a, a forest scene in the movie, but it still looks very nice.

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:22.420
And it just feels like, like there are points where you actually walk through a normal kitchen

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:24.280
and it's not like an endless kitchen.

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:26.460
Right. That's what I thought you were going to mention.

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:30.840
Yeah. That's what it was surprising about the meat freezer thing is like, I actually thought it

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:35.220
would, that would be the other game would have like just had the kitchen kept repeating

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:39.620
until you left the building, but you then go into the meat freezer section and it's like,

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:44.980
you know, another game would have made it like, oh, make sure you equip your, uh, uh, you

00:22:44.980 --> 00:22:48.760
coat or something so that you don't get too cold and take cold damage or something.

00:22:48.940 --> 00:22:52.500
