00:22:52.500 --> 00:22:57.980
And so I agree with you that like this game definitely has, uh, more environments, even,

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.300
even that like they don't do anything to the actual game.

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:01.540
They don't change anything about the game.

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:05.840
And so that's what makes it surprising that you keep kind of going between these, uh, areas.

00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:08.040
Yeah. It gives the levels like a sense of progress.

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:09.240
Like you're progressing through it.

00:23:09.300 --> 00:23:14.000
You're actually going through real places, getting to an actual location, not just like,

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:17.960
have I, have I walked on this endless treadmill long enough to get to the end of the level?

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:56.880
Exactly. All right.

00:23:57.020 --> 00:24:01.120
So then the last two levels, since we're talking about the environments, we might as well stay

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:07.180
on this. On the last two levels, the scale of the environment that you're in kind of changes so that you're in

00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:09.640
